{"status":"ok","message-type":"work","message-version":"1.0.0","message":{"indexed":{"date-parts":[[2026,4,29]],"date-time":"2026-04-29T06:48:16Z","timestamp":1777445296043,"version":"3.51.4"},"reference-count":24,"publisher":"World Scientific Pub Co Pte Ltd","issue":"11","funder":[{"DOI":"10.13039\/501100001809","name":"National Natural Science Foundation of China","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","award":["71871233"],"award-info":[{"award-number":["71871233"]}],"id":[{"id":"10.13039\/501100001809","id-type":"DOI","asserted-by":"publisher"}]},{"name":"National Key Research and Development Project","award":["2017YFD0401001"],"award-info":[{"award-number":["2017YFD0401001"]}]},{"name":"National Key Research and Development Project","award":["2017YFD0700501"],"award-info":[{"award-number":["2017YFD0700501"]}]},{"name":"National Key Research and Development Project","award":["2018YFD0401404"],"award-info":[{"award-number":["2018YFD0401404"]}]},{"DOI":"10.13039\/501100004826","name":"Beijing Natural Science Foundation","doi-asserted-by":"crossref","award":["9182015"],"award-info":[{"award-number":["9182015"]}],"id":[{"id":"10.13039\/501100004826","id-type":"DOI","asserted-by":"crossref"}]}],"content-domain":{"domain":[],"crossmark-restriction":false},"short-container-title":["Mod. Phys. Lett. B"],"published-print":{"date-parts":[[2020,4,20]]},"abstract":"<jats:p> Spectral clustering is one of the most important data processing methods which has been wildly applied to machine learning, computer vision, pattern recognition and image processing. However, one of the main drawbacks of spectral clustering is the fact that the clustering model is defined only for primal data without clear extension to out-of-sample data. To improve its efficiency, in this paper, we proposed a new modularity-based method for spectral clustering with out-of-sample extension. First, kernel independent component analysis is used to solve the demixing matrix on Stiefel manifold in order to extract high-order irrelevant data feature. Then, a new modularity similarity measure-based spectral mapping algorithm is proposed, which allows the clustering model to be directly extended to out-of-sample data. Based on above analysis, we present a spectral clustering algorithm with out-of-sample extension. Experimental results show our method has better performance compared with other related algorithms in different datasets. <\/jats:p>","DOI":"10.1142\/s0217984920501055","type":"journal-article","created":{"date-parts":[[2020,2,5]],"date-time":"2020-02-05T10:39:31Z","timestamp":1580899171000},"page":"2050105","source":"Crossref","is-referenced-by-count":2,"title":["Improve the spectral clustering by integrating a new modularity similarity index and out-of-sample extension"],"prefix":"10.1142","volume":"34","author":[{"given":"Dongqin","family":"Shen","sequence":"first","affiliation":[{"name":"School of Computer Science and Engineering, Nanjing University of Science and Technology, Nanjing 210094, China"}],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]},{"given":"Xiuyi","family":"Li","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"School of Information Engineering, Nanjing University of Finance and Economics, Nanjing 210003, China"}],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]},{"given":"Guan","family":"Yan","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"Academy of Mathematics and Systems Science, Chinese Academy of Sciences, Beijing 100190, China"}],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]}],"member":"219","published-online":{"date-parts":[[2020,2,4]]},"reference":[{"issue":"8","key":"S0217984920501055BIB001","first-page":"888","volume":"22","author":"Shi J.","year":"2002","journal-title":"IEEE T. Pattern Anal."},{"key":"S0217984920501055BIB002","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1016\/j.eswa.2017.10.058"},{"issue":"1","key":"S0217984920501055BIB003","first-page":"50","volume":"4","author":"Hong Y.","year":"2012","journal-title":"Int. J. Adv. Com